{"name":"Cobblestone","hex":"#a89a8e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cobblestone","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rounded stone from a river bed, fit for use as ballast in ships and for paving roads.","Cobblestones viewed as a building or paving material."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cobblestone"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cobblestone","blocks":[{"text":"Cobblestone is a natural building material based on cobble-sized stones, and is used for pavement roads, streets, and buildings. Setts, also called Belgian blocks, are often referred to as \"cobbles\", although a sett is distinct from a cobblestone by being quarried and shaped into a regular form, while cobblestones are naturally occurring rounded forms less uniform in size."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Ancient_road_surface.jpg/330px-Ancient_road_surface.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cobblestone"},{"title":"Cobblestone (magazine)","blocks":[{"text":"Cobblestone is a magazine that is published by Cricket Media and part of Carus Publishing Company."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cobblestone_(magazine)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Cobblestones_%282%29.jpg/500px-Cobblestones_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Cobblestones_%282%29.jpg/1280px-Cobblestones_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Cobblestones_%282%29.jpg/500px-Cobblestones_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sett-paving, such as this surface in Fulham, south-west London, is also often referred to as \"cobblestones\".","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACobblestones_(2).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/London_Cab_of_1823%2C_with_curtain_drawn.png/500px-London_Cab_of_1823%2C_with_curtain_drawn.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/London_Cab_of_1823%2C_with_curtain_drawn.png/500px-London_Cab_of_1823%2C_with_curtain_drawn.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A cabriolet on wet, slippery London cobblestones in 1823","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALondon_Cab_of_1823%2C_with_curtain_drawn.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/ItalianStones.jpg/250px-ItalianStones.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/10/ItalianStones.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/ItalianStones.jpg/250px-ItalianStones.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Italian cobblestone-covered street in Isolabella. Cobblestones such as these are designed for horses to get a good grip.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AItalianStones.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/LT_Kaunas%2C_2019.07.20%2C_fot_Ivonna_Nowicka_%283%29.jpg/500px-LT_Kaunas%2C_2019.07.20%2C_fot_Ivonna_Nowicka_%283%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/LT_Kaunas%2C_2019.07.20%2C_fot_Ivonna_Nowicka_%283%29.jpg/1280px-LT_Kaunas%2C_2019.07.20%2C_fot_Ivonna_Nowicka_%283%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/LT_Kaunas%2C_2019.07.20%2C_fot_Ivonna_Nowicka_%283%2